# lifecycle audit lane LC1 (2026-11-24). Written against the Feature text with sha b19fb85071aeacd3; honest subset only: nothing about a real sleep is checked.
row: F-LIFE-21
targets: qemu
profile: ram
feature-sha: b19fb85071aeacd3
doc: the Power page of Settings states what sleep, idle sleep and the power button do
clause: 1 the Power page of Settings shows the idle sleep and the power button cards with their words
not-covered: a real sleep, a lid, or the lock that sleep puts first (a QEMU guest has no lid and no sleep state)
not-covered: that a running install or job holds sleep back
key s
wait app=Settings
skip-unless-button Power
click-sidebar Power
wait app=Settings page=Power
shot page
expect-not-blank
expect-text Sleep when idle
expect-text Power button
expect-page Power
